SteamARM: FEX's code buffer as a Darwin MAP_JIT region with per-thread write scopes, the way the
Linux ELF build of FEX runs under the runtime (patches/fex-lxrt-wx.patch, same scope sites). Wine
commits the PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE buffer with mprotect, which the runtime splits W^X page by page:
every compiled block cost a write flip and an execute flip of a 16 KiB page, ~6,500 of each per
second in Minecraft Dungeons II. The buffer is adopted as MAP_JIT right after allocation (private
syscall 0x4C580020, enable=3); without thread_local, the runtime counts nested scopes.

